---
title: "Study Groups"
description: "ISC2 certification study groups forming now in Tampa Bay — CISSP, CCSP, SSCP, CGRC, CSSLP."
layout: base.njk
---

  <!-- Page Header -->
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Study Groups</h1>
      <p class="page-header-subtitle">CISSP, CCSP, SSCP — study together, pass together.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Overview -->
  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-label">Launching now</span>
      <h2>Don't prep alone</h2>
      <p>We're spinning up study groups for ISC2 certifications. If you're preparing for <strong>CISSP, CCSP, SSCP, CGRC, or CSSLP</strong>, you shouldn't be doing it alone.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why study groups work -->
  <section class="content-section" style="background: var(--light-gray);">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-label">Why it works</span>
      <h2>Three reasons to study with a group</h2>
      <ul class="benefits-list">
        <li><strong>Accountability.</strong> You show up because other people are counting on you.</li>
        <li><strong>Shared resources.</strong> Someone in the group has already found the good flashcards.</li>
        <li><strong>Different perspectives.</strong> A cloud engineer and a network defender read the same domain differently, and that's the point.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What we're planning -->
  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-label">The plan</span>
      <h2>What we're putting together</h2>
      <ul class="benefits-list">
        <li><strong>CISSP study group</strong> — our flagship. Weekly or bi-weekly, likely hybrid (in-person + virtual).</li>
        <li><strong>CCSP, SSCP, CGRC, CSSLP</strong> — depending on interest. Tell us which one you want and we'll try to get enough people together.</li>
        <li><strong>Format</strong> — sessions before or after quarterly chapter meetings, plus virtual check-ins in between.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Sign up form -->
  <section class="content-section" id="signup" style="background: var(--light-gray);">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-label">Sign up</span>
      <h2>Tell us you're interested</h2>
      <p>Drop your email and we'll reach out when a group forms. Already a subscriber? You'll still get the study-group tag applied so we know to include you.</p>

      <form class="subscribe-form study-group-form" data-source="study-groups" novalidate>
        <label for="studyGroupEmail" class="sr-only">Email address</label>
        <div class="subscribe-form-row">
          <input type="email" id="studyGroupEmail" name="email" placeholder="your@email.com" autocomplete="email" required>
          <button type="submit" class="btn subscribe-submit">Sign Me Up</button>
        </div>
        <div class="cf-turnstile" data-sitekey="{{ site.turnstile.siteKey }}"></div>
        <p class="subscribe-feedback" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
      </form>

      <div class="callout" style="margin-top: 24px;">
        <p style="margin:0;"><strong>Already certified?</strong> We could use experienced CISSPs and CCSPs as group leaders and occasional guest coaches. Email <a href="mailto:membership@isc2chapter-tampabay.org?subject=Study%20Group%20Leader">membership@isc2chapter-tampabay.org</a> with subject "Study Group Leader" — helps us, counts as Group A CPEs for you.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="cta-banner">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Ready to start studying together?</h2>
      <p class="cta-subtitle">Sign up above and we'll be in touch when a group forms around your cert.</p>
      <div class="cta-banner-actions">
        <a href="#signup" class="btn">Sign Up</a>
        <a href="/cpe/" class="btn-outline btn-outline--light">See CPE Info</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>